    "study.r.papel.r2": "No access to users while building, so the audience and the problem remain hypotheses.",
    "study.r.papel.r3": "Front end in a single HTML file, with React and Tailwind loaded from a CDN and no build step.",
    "study.r.papel.r4": "No account server: data stays in each person’s browser.",
    "study.r.decisoes.titulo": "UX decisions and rationale",
    "study.r.decisoes.intro": "Each decision below has a design rationale and a point that still needs to be validated with people.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d1-titulo": "Modules unlocked in order",
    "study.r.decisoes.d1-texto": "People studying alone don’t need to decide the sequence: the next module is highlighted and the following ones stay locked.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d1-validar": "<strong>To validate.</strong> Locking may frustrate people who already know the subject. It’s one of the tasks in the test plan.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d2-titulo": "Progress comes from focus time",
    "study.r.decisoes.d2-texto": "Hours, sessions, and streak are calculated from logged sessions, not from items checked by hand, to reflect real effort.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d2-validar": "<strong>To validate.</strong> I don’t know whether people understand what counts as a study day.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d3-titulo": "A pre-session screen instead of a timer on Home",
    "study.r.decisoes.d3-texto": "A session starts on a screen that sets the plan and duration, and a floating timer follows the person around the app.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d3-validar": "<strong>To validate.</strong> The session is now one step further from Home. I need to see whether people find it.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d4-titulo": "“Ofensiva” with a caption",
    "study.r.decisoes.d4-texto": "“Streak” became “Ofensiva”, with a sentence that explains the term, because a Portuguese name isn’t enough when the concept is new.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d4-validar": "<strong>To validate.</strong> I haven’t tested whether the term is understood without help.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d8-titulo": "AI failure as part of the flow",
    "study.r.decisoes.d8-texto": "Every generated piece of content has a loading state, an error message in plain language, and a Try again button. Details in <a class=\"link\" href=\"#ia\">AI, errors, and states</a>.",
    "study.r.decisoes.d8-validar": "<strong>To validate.</strong> I haven’t measured how long people are willing to wait for a generation.",
    "study.r.ds.intro": "I designed the interface in Figma, and in the product the visual decisions became tokens and reusable components. The inventory below was taken from the published code in October 2026. It describes what exists, not a complete library. <span class=\"tag tag--done\">Implemented</span>",
