    "study.r.validacao.status-texto": "Usability tests planned, not yet conducted. No session has taken place and there are no results. When there are, they’ll be added here with the date, number of participants, and limitations.",
    "study.r.validacao.objetivo": "Goal",
    "study.r.validacao.objetivo-v": "See whether people who study on their own can, without help, pick a topic, study the first module, run a focus session, and understand their own progress.",
    "study.r.validacao.formato": "Format",
    "study.r.validacao.formato-v": "Moderated test, remote or in person, with five people, on the public demo, using think-aloud. About 40 minutes per session.",
    "study.r.validacao.perfil": "Participants",
    "study.r.validacao.perfil-v": "People who study something on their own, such as a language or for an exam, on their phone, at least twice a week. No designers or people close to the project.",
    "study.r.validacao.metricas": "What I’ll observe",
    "study.r.validacao.metricas-v": "Completion of each task without help, time per task, errors and hesitations, understanding of “Ofensiva” and of module locking, and an ease rating from 1 to 7 per task.",
    "study.r.validacao.priorizacao": "<strong>How I’ll prioritize what comes up.</strong> Each problem gets a severity from 0 to 4, based on how many participants hit it, its impact on the task, and whether the person works around it alone. I’ll first fix what blocks the task, then what repeats across more than one person. With five participants, the findings point to problems but don’t measure how often they happen in general.",
    "study.r.metricas.titulo": "Metrics I would track",
    "study.r.metricas.intro": "None of these metrics has been measured. The app doesn’t collect usage data yet, so there is no baseline, and I didn’t set numeric targets so as not to confuse wishes with results.",
