    "cc.r.alt.intro": "The alternatives explored during the original project weren’t documented, so I don’t reconstruct them from memory. The two below were considered later, in October 2026, and are recorded as next experiments.",
    "cc.r.alt.a1-t": "Five tabs, with Movies",
    "cc.r.alt.a1-p": "Follow the taxonomy strictly: Home, Movies, Tickets, Club, and Profile. It gains direct access to the catalog; it loses space and goes back to five items, the same number as the current app.",
    "cc.r.alt.a1-v": "<strong>How to decide.</strong> A navigation A/B test or a tree test with both structures.",
    "cc.r.alt.a2-t": "Extras inside payment",
    "cc.r.alt.a2-p": "Offer combos as an optional block in payment instead of a step. It would leave three steps, but may hide a revenue source for the chain.",
    "cc.r.alt.a2-v": "<strong>How to decide.</strong> Compare time to pay and how many people notice the combos in the prototype.",
    "cc.r.alt.tag": "Revision alternative",
    "cc.r.solucao.titulo": "Before and after",
    "cc.r.a11y.intro": "I calculated the contrast of the design system’s color pairs with the WCAG formula. It isn’t a full audit: I didn’t test with a screen reader or with people.",
